I stand at the till.
I take the groceries out of the basket.
I place the cheese and the kohlrabi on the conveyor belt.
I also place the apples on the belt.
The cashier scans everything.
"That is twenty-five Euro, please," he says.
I have no change.
I only have a fifty-Euro note.
The cashier takes the banknote.
I take the change.
"Would you like the receipt?" he asks.
I do not like so much paper.
"No, thank you, I do not need a receipt," I answer.
I pack the groceries into my bags.
That takes a moment.
The cashier does not wait long.
He is already scanning for the next person.
"Have a nice day," he says.
"Thank you, you too," I say.
I take the bags and go to the exit.
